goto_ptr per-TB inline cache (2026-09-11, REJECTED: flat)

The emitted lookup_and_goto_ptr computed the ARM lookup key (pc, hflags, cs_base
with THUMB/CONDEXEC/VECLEN/VECSTRIDE/VFPEN) inline and tail-called a one-entry
per-TB cache of the last resolution (validated: CF_INVALID, fidx, chain brake).
Hit rate 80 % (57.8M hits / 14.9M misses per boot, 1.75M lookups/s) but idlebench
--quick both orders vs the session base: t1.3G ratios 0.824/0.864 with it,
0.823/0.844 without; t0.5G 0.893/0.940 vs 0.900/0.915 — the inline key
computation costs about what the helper's jump-cache probe saves.
Applies on top of 0030 with: git apply patches/attic/goto-ptr-inline-cache.diff

